      "writtenOn": "2024-11-15T00:10:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, right the change in `common/queue_policies.c`.\n\nBack to that file specifically:\n\n```\nvoid queue_add_direct(struct queue_policy const *policy, size_t count)\n{\n...\n\tif (direct-\u003econsumer-\u003eops-\u003ewritten)  \u003c\u003c---- count check removed\n\t\tdirect-\u003econsumer-\u003eops-\u003ewritten(direct-\u003econsumer, count);\n}\n```\n\nFor my own sake, this portion of your commit message is referring to the implementations of `direct-\u003econsumer-\u003eops-\u003ewritten()`?\n\n\u003e Some consumers will not know about the flushing semantics, but that is\n\u003e fine, they will ignore a notification with zero length, and they will\n\u003e eagerly process data, which is always allowed.",
      "parentUuid": "78b60deb_66ccd29b",
      "revId": "014b04c3b006a3cdec86eec1f45410caf613dd1a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
