      "writtenOn": "2024-11-15T15:39:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Correct.  These existing implementations of `written()` will probably either unconditioinally wake up some task, which will then consume any bytes available in the queue, or they will run an iteration based on the `count` parameter.  It will be harmless if they should be woken up by the new `queue_flush()` function making a call with zero `count`.",
      "parentUuid": "c91351cd_a03cb3de",
      "revId": "014b04c3b006a3cdec86eec1f45410caf613dd1a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
